// Cells: the ground plan, then SilNebula's stamps (games/silice/gfx/SilNebula.ron, original art).
// Ground legend: . the city paving (512), m the Tower esplanade's black marble (541), b the grey
// concrete of the Quai des Eaux Grises and the Bassin's rim (542), q the quai's edge over the canal
// (543), ~ water (General 368, Surf), D d deep water (General 334/335, Dive); A B C E the glass and
// steel tower blocks (513-516, by cell parity), S T their ground floor (517-518), V W X Y the
// Tower's black glass (519-522), = the yellow Cocket barricades (608), - | the Bassin's fence
// (609, 610), g its open gate (611, the Bassin guard stands on it), p the plastic flower planters
// (629, walkable; the hidden PP Up).
// North (y 3-13): the esplanade of black marble before the Tower (x 24-33), the Grande Porte
// (26-31, 8-10), its locked laser gate at (28-29, 10); the west avenue (12-13, 3-13) is barred by the
// barricade (x 14). The north wall (14-23, 3) is the towers' ground floor; Nebula_OnLoad draws the
// Breach's crack at (18-19, 3) from VAR_SIL_STORY 126 (General's cave mouth 167).
// East (x 44-57, y 3-21): the Bassin de Captage behind its fence, the gate at (44, 12), deep water
// (Dive) at (50-52, 10-13). The east avenue (53-57, 28-33) is barred by the barricade (x 52).
// Centre (y 14-41): the giant screen (27-33, 18-21) on its tower, the Place de l'Ecran, the Center
// (16-18, 31-33) west and the Comptoir (41-43, 31-33) east.
// West (x 2-13): the residential towers; the Gargote (4-6, 29-31) and the MAINTENANCE door (10-12,
// 17-18, door (11, 18), locked) at the end of the alley.
// South (y 46-56): the Quai des Eaux Grises over the canal (y 49-56); deep water (Dive) at (29-30, 54-55).
